-- title:
--   Archimedean twisted weighted orbital germ expansion in (t,a)
-- statement:
--   Let $K\subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of $L$ over $K$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and assume $[L:K]$ is prime. Let $\varphi_\infty:\mathrm{GL}_2(L_\infty)\to\mathbb C$ be an archimedean test factor, i.e. $\varphi_\infty$ has compact support and is of the form $g\mapsto \Phi$ applied to the matrix entries of $g$ read in the mixed space of $L$, for some smooth $\Phi$, and let $\tau_0$ be a measure on $K_\infty\times K_\infty$ (the infinite adele ring of $K$ carrying its Borel structure). The assertion is the existence of a function $B$ and families $C_w,E_w$ indexed by the infinite places $w$ of $K$, all from $(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\to$ mixed space of $K$ to $\mathbb C$, all smooth of infinite order over $\mathbb R$ and compactly supported, such that: at every point where one of $B$, $C_w$, $E_w$ is nonzero both coordinates come from units of $K_\infty$ under the ring isomorphism $K_\infty\cong$ mixed space; there is a compact set $C_a$ of pairs of units of $K_\infty$ whose image contains the union of the closed supports of $B$ and of all $C_w,E_w$; all these functions vanish at $(t,a)$ whenever $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ is not a norm, that is, whenever no $\delta$ and $y$ satisfy $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)_{L\otimes K_\infty}=y^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma(\delta)\cdots\sigma^{[L:K]-1}(\delta)\,y$; and, writing $\nu(t)=\prod_{w}\bigl(\|1-t_w\|/\sqrt{\|t_w\|}\bigr)^{m_w}$ with $m_w$ the local degree, for all units $a,t$ of $K_\infty$ with $\gamma=\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ regular semisimple (meaning $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2-4\det(\gamma)$ is a unit), for every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$ whose push-forward under the two diagonal entries is $\tau_0$, for all units $\alpha,\beta$ of $L\otimes_K K_\infty$ with $\sigma$-norm string of $\delta=\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta)$ equal to the image of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_\infty)$, for every Haar measure $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta$ coupled to $\tau$ with conjugator $1$, and for all $J',I'\in\mathbb C$ such that $J'$ is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_\infty\circ\mathrm{archIdentGL}$ at $\delta$ against the Haar measure `archHaarL` with weight $y\mapsto -\log H^L_\infty(y)-\log H^L_\infty(w\,y)$ ($H^L_\infty$ the archimedean height, $w$ the image of the adelic Weyl element) and $I'$ is the corresponding unweighted twisted orbital integral, one has $$\nu(t)J'=-2\,[L:K]\Bigl(\sum_w m_w\log\|1-t_w\|\Bigr)\,\nu(t)I'+B(\iota t,\iota a)+\sum_{w\ \mathrm{real}}\|1-t_w\|\,C_w(\iota t,\iota a)+\sum_{w\ \mathrm{complex}}\|1-t_w\|^2\log\|1-t_w\|\,E_w(\iota t,\iota a),$$ where $\iota$ denotes the mixed-space coordinates and the arguments are the pair $(t,a)$ in that order.
--
--   This is the archimedean germ, or kink, expansion on the $L$-side of the twisted trace formula comparison: the weighted twisted orbital integral at a split regular class $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ equals $-2[L:K]\sum_w m_w\log\|1-t_w\|$ times the unweighted one, up to smooth compactly supported error terms in the pair $(t,a)$ of unit coordinates, with the real and complex places contributing errors of size $\|1-t\|$ and $\|1-t\|^2\log\|1-t\|$ respectively. It is stated globally in $(t,a)$ so as to feed the comparison of the weighted archimedean discrepancy with $[L:K]$ times the $K$-side weighted integral.
